     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Shared information",
     "texto": [
      "**-잖아요** presents information as shared or recognisable: 가다 → **가잖아요**, 먹다 → **먹잖아요**, 좋다 → **좋잖아요**. Depending on the context, it can remind someone of an agreement, justify an opinion or correct something.",
      "오늘 같이 점심 **먹잖아요** = we are eating lunch together today, you know."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Tone",
     "texto": [
      "It can sound friendly, insistent or slightly complaining if used to remind someone of something. It is not always a complaint: the tone and the relationship between the speakers matter.",
      "어제 **말했잖아요** = I already told you yesterday."
